Vendored artifact
-----------------
    src/font_split/data/lang-unicodes.json

Derived from these upstream files (`crates/lang_unicodes/`):

    src/lib.rs             area table: 32 language areas, their ranges and order
    src/cjk_unicodes.rs    Hiragana/Katakana and Hangul Jamo ranges
    build.rs               CN_SYMBOL (Chinese punctuation) and CN_CHARS (Chinese
                           character frequency list, 6767 characters)
    scripts/syl-2.txt      Korean syllable frequency list (2026 syllables)

Upstream reference: commit 1650af130b8c547b13a883ac7546f088ff193bf5

The traditional-Chinese area (`ZH_TC` / tag `han-t`) is not shipped upstream as a
list: upstream derives it by converting the frequency list to traditional Chinese
with OpenCC (`Config::S2T`). `tools/gen_lang_data.py` performs the same derivation
with the Python OpenCC dictionaries, keeping only characters that differ from the
simplified list and that fit in the BMP (2303 characters).

Regenerating
------------
    uv run --group dev python tools/gen_lang_data.py

The generator only downloads from the pinned commit above and requires the `opencc`
dictionary beyond the runtime dependencies. Its output is committed, so a normal
build never touches the network.
